<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 9.999 percent from 9.997 percent at the previous auction on February 3.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Aug 19, 1997 (Aug 5, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.999 percent (9.997)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 767.800 million (702.375 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 870.500 million (902.375 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.800-10.101 percent (9.380-10.101)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.380-10.500 percent (9.380-10.300)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 154 (124)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 158 (126)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1 REUTER MS</p>
